<title>ESTONIA: HOIU TO ORDER CREDIT RATING.</title>
<headline>HOIU TO ORDER CREDIT RATING.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, Estonia's third largest bank, said on Monday that it had decided to order a credit rating. </p>
<p>&quot;It is clear that we will order the rating, there is no doubt,&quot; Priit Haller, the bank's vice-chairman, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Hoiupank will decide on Tuesday or Wednesday whether it will choose one agency or ask for indications from different agencies and pick up an agency based on those results, he added.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
